<header>
    <h1>KCSE University & College Transition Guide</h1>
    <p>Step-by-step instructions for Results, KUCCPS Placement, SSP & HELB Funding</p>
</header>

<div class="container">

    <!-- PAYMENT PROMPT SECTION -->
    <div id="paywall-box">
        <span class="badge">INSTANT ACCESS</span>
        <h2>Unlock the Complete Student Application Guide</h2>
        <p>Get clear, accurate instructions to avoid costly application mistakes.</p>
        <div class="price-tag">KES 100</div>
        
        <ul class="features-list">
            <li><strong>1. KCSE Results:</strong> Official KNEC portal & SMS checking steps.</li>
            <li><strong>2. KUCCPS Portal:</strong> How to calculate cluster weights & select courses.</li>
            <li><strong>3. SSP (Self-Sponsored):</strong> How to apply directly to universities if you miss placement.</li>
            <li><strong>4. HELB & HEF Portal:</strong> First-time loan & scholarship application checklist.</li>
        </ul>

        <!-- PAYSTACK POPUP BUTTON -->
        <button class="pay-btn" onclick="payWithPaystack()">Pay KES 100 via M-Pesa / Card</button>

        <!-- MANUAL M-PESA TILL FALLBACK -->
        <div class="manual-verify">
            <p><strong>Alternative:</strong> Send <strong>KES 100</strong> to M-Pesa Till/Phone: <strong>07XX XXX XXX</strong><br>
            Enter the 10-character M-Pesa Transaction Code below to unlock:</p>
            <input type="text" id="mpesa-code" placeholder="e.g. SLK89X21MP" maxlength="10">
            <button class="verify-btn" onclick="verifyManualCode()">Unlock Guide</button>
            <p id="error-msg" style="color: red; display: none; margin-top: 8px;"></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PROTECTED GUIDE SECTION -->
    <div id="premium-guide">
        <div style="background: #d4edda; color: #155724; padding: 15px; border-radius: 6px; margin-bottom: 20px; text-align: center;">
            <strong>Payment Confirmed!</strong> Bookmark this page or take screenshots for reference.
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 1: KCSE RESULTS -->
        <div class="guide-card">
            <span class="badge">STEP 1</span>
            <h2>How to Check KCSE Results</h2>
            <p>KNEC phases out old SMS shortcodes periodically and uses the official online portal:</p>
            <ol>
                <li>Visit the official KNEC results portal: <strong>results.knec.ac.ke</strong></li>
                <li>Enter your <strong>11-digit KCSE Index Number</strong> (without spaces or slashes).</li>
                <li>Enter your <strong>registered name</strong> (at least one name as it appears on your registration slip).</li>
                <li>Click <strong>Submit / View Results</strong> to display your provisional slip.</li>
                <li><em>Tip:</em> Always collect your official printed result slip from your former high school for university registration.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 2: KUCCPS APPLICATION -->
        <div class="guide-card">
            <span class="badge">STEP 2</span>
            <h2>How to Apply for Schools via KUCCPS</h2>
            <p>Once KUCCPS opens the student portal (usually between March and April):</p>
            <ol>
                <li>Go to <strong>students.kuccps.net</strong> and click <strong>Login</strong>.</li>
                <li>Use your <strong>KCSE Index Number</strong>, <strong>KCSE Year</strong>, and your <strong>KCPE Index Number</strong> (or Birth Certificate Number) as the initial password.</li>
                <li>Check your <strong>Cluster Weights</strong> under the "Programmes" tab. Compare your points against the previous year's cut-off points.</li>
                <li>Select <strong>4 Degree Choices</strong> (1a, 1b, 1c, 2, 3, 4) or Diploma/Certificate courses depending on your mean grade (C+ and above for Degree; C- and above for Diploma).</li>
                <li>Pay the <strong>KES 1,500</strong> KUCCPS application fee via the M-Pesa eCitizen prompt generated on the portal and submit before the deadline.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 3: SSP APPLICATION -->
        <div class="guide-card">
            <span class="badge">STEP 3</span>
            <h2>How to Apply via SSP (Self-Sponsored Programme)</h2>
            <p>If you miss your preferred course through KUCCPS or want to join immediately as a parallel/self-sponsored student:</p>
            <ol>
                <li>Visit the specific university's official admissions portal (e.g., <em>application.uonbi.ac.ke</em>, <em>ku.ac.ke</em>, <em>jkuat.ac.ke</em>, <em>mku.ac.ke</em>).</li>
                <li>Create an applicant account and select <strong>Self-Sponsored / Module II / Privately Sponsored</strong> intake (usually May or September).</li>
                <li>Upload scanned PDF copies of your <strong>KCSE Result Slip, KCPE Certificate, National ID/Birth Certificate, and Passport Photo</strong>.</li>
                <li>Pay the university's non-refundable application fee (typically KES 1,000 – KES 2,000) via their official bank/M-Pesa paybill.</li>
                <li>Download your admission letter once approved. Note that SSP students can still apply for HELB loans.</li>
            </ol>
        </div>

        <!-- SECTION 4: HELB & HEF APPLICATION -->
        <div class="guide-card">
            <span class="badge">STEP 4</span>
            <h2>How to Apply for HELB Loan & Government Scholarship (HEF)</h2>
            <p>Under the Student-Centred Funding Model, both scholarships and loans are applied for on one portal:</p>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Required Documents:</strong> Your National ID (or Maisha Card), valid email, Safaricom phone number registered in your name, KRA PIN, bank account or M-Pesa details, Parents' IDs & KRA PINs, and 2 Guarantors' IDs & phone numbers.</li>
                <li>Visit <strong>portal.hef.co.ke</strong> (or download the <strong>HELB App</strong> from Google Play Store).</li>
                <li>Register an account using your ID number and verify your email/phone.</li>
